  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), む-ending.\n- Negative: {澄|す}まない\n- Polite: {澄|す}みます\n- Te-form: {澄|す}んで\n- Past: {澄|す}んだ\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in the ている form ({澄|す}んでいる) to describe a state of clarity. The compound {澄|す}みわたる means \"to be perfectly clear throughout.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {水|みず}が{澄|す}む: the water becomes clear\n- {空気|くうき}が{澄|す}む: the air becomes clear\n- {澄|す}んだ{目|め}: clear eyes\n- {澄|す}んだ{声|こえ}: a clear voice\n- {澄|す}みわたる: to be perfectly clear",
